invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh p256-equiv
reason: the form of the subtract with borrow that gcc reads for x86-64
  hands _subborrow_u64 its two words in the other order, so it returns
  b - a - borrow where the step is a - b - borrow. CBMC reads no
  intrinsic, so no proof covers the form, and clang reads another, so on
  a machine whose compiler is clang no test binary compiles the line.
  The script builds bin/p256_equiv_test for x86-64 on the intrinsics and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64, where it holds every difference to
  p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    *borrow = _subborrow_u64((unsigned char)*borrow, a, b, &difference);
--- new
    *borrow = _subborrow_u64((unsigned char)*borrow, b, a, &difference);
